-- The voice of the corn poppy. Dreamy and drowsy, wistful but warm, a bright
-- brief red flower who lives wholly in the present day. Yawns, drifts, talks
-- of sleep, dreams, waking and remembering, and now and then calls the reader
-- dreamer. Each flower lasts a day or two and the plant keeps opening new
-- ones through the summer; the seeds sleep in the soil for years and wake
-- when the ground is turned. Winter is spent asleep as seed, never gone.
-- The memories tell of a long sleep, a plough, a pepper pot, a paper poppy,
-- a pressed flower, a voice heard through the soil and a spade.
-- (garden/voice.lua says how a voice is written.)

